From: CustomDrumDestroyer <350583592+CustomDrumDestroyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ui/cocoa: drag and drop, Resize Guest with Window (rv530)

The Cocoa side of 0003 and 0004, for macOS hosts:
- with RV530_DND_SEND set (snowleopard/sl-vm.sh DND=1), files dropped on
  the window are handed to "CMD --at X,Y PATH..." with the drop point in
  guest pixels; when the pointer leaves the window with the button held
  while the guest drags files ("CMD --query"), a host drag starts whose
  file URLs come from "CMD --fetch", and when it ends the guest's drag is
  cancelled with Escape, the button released 300 ms later (the keyboard
  and the tablet are separate USB devices);
- for a display device with a run-time "auto-resize" property, View >
  Resize Guest with Window switches whether the guest resolution follows
  the window (turning Zoom To Fit on when needed); while it does, the
  window has no aspect lock and takes the size of a new guest mode until
  it is resized by anyone else (a mode the guest passes through would
  otherwise become the next request);
- for such a device a resizable window reports its size in points, not
  pixels, so a Retina window does not ask for twice its size.
